    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i've been having this weird heavy feeling in my jaw and kinda down my neck for the last hour or so. it's not even chest pain or anything, just a dull ache. i think i might just be clenching my teeth from stress or something, but wanted to check if there's any reason to worry about it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hello! It sounds like your muscles might be tense due to stress, which is causing this sensation. While it's often linked to stress, dental issues can also be a cause, especially if you have recent dental work or are prone to teeth grinding. If the feeling persists or worsens, or you have concerns about underlying causes like a muscle spasm or dental issues, I would recommend seeing a healthcare professional for an accurate diagnosis and appropriate treatment. In the meantime, you might find some relief using warm compresses, practicing relaxation techniques, and avoiding hard or chewy foods.",
