      "content": "Muscle tension related to stress usually doesn't require emergency care, but it's essential to listen to your body. Since you don't feel any other severe symptoms and this discomfort seems to be purely muscular, it may indeed resolve on its own or get relieved through self-care strategies. However, if your symptoms do not improve, become significantly worse, or are accompanied by other symptoms such as difficulty swallowing, facial droop, or sharp, persistent pain, it would be wise to seek medical attention. Considering potential dental causes, speaking with your dentist could help rule out any related issues that might be exacerbating your discomfort. Self-care is fine for mild cases, but always err on the side of caution with any unexplained medical concerns.",
